-- ============================================================================
-- DC13 - Basin and Charge Beginner (Associate) goes deep.
--
-- Flips (basin, beginner) onto the DC1 deep path by inserting its ACTIVE
-- academy_course_structures row, generated from the repo manifest
-- src/content/courses/basin/beginner/manifest.json (the structure source
-- of truth; this file was emitted by a generator, not hand-typed), and
-- seeding the module quiz banks (15+15+15+15+15+15 questions) plus the
-- 42-question final exam bank. Answer keys live only here and in the
-- table (no client SELECT policies); the repo lesson content carries no
-- graded questions.
--
-- Every numeric question traces to the basin teaching oracle and
-- reproduces the live NG11 Beginner capstone answer key: Sclater-Christie
-- compaction and decompaction plus the golden two-layer steady heat
-- column (solid thickness in 100 m of surface shale 38.57953418711555 m,
-- 100 m shale from 1000 m restored to 159.79553483785466 m, shale
-- porosity at 2000 m 0.22717481230903933, and the column read at 50 m
-- 11.666666666666671, at 950 m 41.66666666666673 and at 1950 m
-- 59.619047619047684 degC). The fixtures are committed goldens with an
-- independent stdlib-Python oracle. That is the same pipeline
-- src/lib/basinTeaching.js drives and src/components/course/panels/
-- basin/burialHeatLab.test.js pins.
--
-- Scope note: the Beginner tier is burial and heat only. Maturity
-- kinetics belong to the Professional tier, and the full forward model,
-- generation, expulsion and the erosion signature to the Expert tier.
--
-- Bank standard: this bank was measured on the length RANK of the
-- correct option before seeding, per the standard introduced with DC12
-- (see migrations/docs/bank-length-cue-reseed-pentest.md).
--
-- Enrollment grandfathering: enforced_from defaults to now() on first
-- insert, so learners enrolled before this apply finish on the old path;
-- the ON CONFLICT update deliberately leaves enforced_from unchanged on
-- re-seeds. Re-seeding replaces the whole bank for this course-tier;
-- fine while there are no open attempts (open attempts pin question ids).
-- ============================================================================

values ('basin', 'beginner', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-why-basin-modelling","title":"Why Basin Modelling","lesson_keys":["l01-the-question-a-basin-model-answers","l02-the-petroleum-system","l03-the-golden-fixtures","l04-the-beginner-scope"]},{"key":"m02-compaction","title":"Compaction","lesson_keys":["l01-porosity-falls-with-depth","l02-the-sclater-christie-curve","l03-porosity-at-depth","l04-solid-thickness","l05-lithology-changes-the-curve"]},{"key":"m03-decompaction","title":"Decompaction","lesson_keys":["l01-what-decompaction-is","l02-restoring-a-buried-layer","l03-grain-is-conserved","l04-why-burial-history-needs-it"]},{"key":"m04-heat-in-the-subsurface","title":"Heat in the Subsurface","lesson_keys":["l01-heat-flow-and-conductivity","l02-the-steady-state-column","l03-two-layers-two-gradients","l04-reading-the-column"]},{"key":"m05-burial-and-heat-together","title":"Burial and Heat Together","lesson_keys":["l01-a-layer-has-a-history","l02-why-time-and-temperature-both-matter","l03-what-this-tier-does-not-do","l04-sanity-checks"]},{"key":"m06-the-basin-workflow","title":"The Basin Workflow","lesson_keys":["l01-the-workflow-end-to-end","l02-quality-control","l03-the-capstone-walkthrough","l04-onward-to-professional"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
